  "text_pages": [
    "Dong-A University Office Of  External International  Affairs > Korean Language Course > Application Procedure\n스킵네비게이션\n본문바로가기\n주메뉴바로가기\nAdmission\nDONG-A UNIVERSITY, WHERE WE MAKE YOUR HISTORY\n메인으로 이동\nAdmission\nOffice of International Affairs\nAdmission\nGlobal Network\nInternational Relations Programs\nInternational Student Support\nBulletin Boards\n닫기\nKorean Language Course\nKorean Language Course\nUndergraduate_Korean Track\nUndergraduate_English Track\nGraduate\n닫기\nAdmission\nAdmission\nKorean Language Course\nUndergraduate_Korean Track\nOverview\nScholarships\nAdmission guidelines\nApply Link\nContact\nUndergraduate_English Track\nOverview\nScholarships\nAdmission guidelines\nApply Link\nContact\nGraduate\nAcademic Programs\nKorean Track\nEnglish Track\nChina Track\nScholarships\nKorean Track\nEnglish Track\nKorean Language Course\nSNS 목록열기\nFACEBOOK 공유하기\nTWITTER 공유하기\nBLOG 공유하기\nSNS 목록닫기\n인쇄\nurl 복사\nOverview and Class Schedule\nTeaching Method and Curriculum\nSpecial Activities and Registration Information\nApplication Procedure\nContact Information\nApplication Process\nApplication Requirements\nHigh school graduates or those with equivalent educational background (applicable to those planning to enter a new university)\nhose who can obtain the status of residence of language training and study abroad according to the Immigration Law.\nApplication Procedures\nSubmission of support documents and payment of support fee (by mail or in person)\nAfter screening of documents, individual applicants will be notified of the results.\nPayment of the full amount of the training fee in the applicant's name and notification of the fact of payment to the school (by fax or phone)\nAfter confirming the payment, the school issues an admission letter and a certificate of payment of course fees, and sends them to the applicant.\nApply for visa with the documents received (for Chinese students, the school is in charge of visa application)\nAfter receiving the visa, the applicant enters Japan.\nLevel test\nApplication Documents\nDocuments to be submitted : All documents must be submitted in original by mail or in person.\nCommon documents (domestic resident status holders submit common documents only)\nDocuments to be submitted\nRemarks\nApplication Form for Korean Language Courses at Dong-A University\nDownload\nCertificate of final education\nAcademic background verification is required\nCopy of passport and Alien Registration Card\nAlien Registration Card must be submitted by the applicant.\nIdentification photo\n5 photos (3cm x 4cm) - white background\nSelection fee\n50,000 won (non-refundable)\nAdditional documents for students residing abroad\nStudy Plan\nProof of bank balance of at least 8,000,000KRW\nCertificate of employment and proof of income of the guardian in home country\nCertificate of family relationship (only a copy of family register if all family relations are shown in the family register for Chinese nationals)\nPhotocopies of the parent's and guardian's ID cards (ID card that confirms nationality)\nTranscript of academic records\nTuberculosis certificate (for applicants residing in a high-risk country)\nDocuments written in foreign languages other than English or Chinese must be submitted together with a Korean or English translation.\nDocuments may be added or subtracted as necessary.\nNotes\nApplicants with academic background/degree in China : The documents must be submitted with the report of certification of academic background/degree, etc. issued by the Center for Certification of Academic Background and Degree, which is operated by the Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China.\nMethod of Certifying Educational Background of Chinese High School Graduates\nGeneral high school graduates (choose from the following)\nGao Kao (High School Examination, University Entrance Examination) score report (certified by the Ministry of Education) and graduation certificate (issued by the principal of t